    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n150 Aylmer Road presents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a spacious and versatile family home, ideally positioned within easy walking distance of Newcastle Village. This attractive property offers well-proportioned accommodation extending over two floors, with three bedrooms upstairs and generous extended living accommodation at ground-floor level. \nA particular feature of the property is the superb fully insulated, wired and plumbed chalet-style garden room, providing an exceptional additional space suitable for extended family, guests, working from home, a home gym or a variety of other uses. The property also enjoys an enviable outlook over agricultural tillage lands to the rear, a rare and highly desirable feature in the Newcastle market.\nUpon entering the property, you are greeted by a spacious entrance hall, featuring attractive laminate flooring and useful under-stairs storage. To the front of the property, the original living room has been thoughtfully reconfigured to incorporate a large and practical fully tiled wet room. This bathroom is fitted with an electric shower, WC and wash hand basin\nThe living room itself remains a spacious and comfortable reception area, featuring a large picture window and attractive feature fireplace.\nContinuing through the hallway towards the rear of the property is a further generous family room extending across the full width of the house. Centred around a feature fireplace, this bright and versatile room provides excellent family and entertaining space. Double doors open directly from this living area onto the rear patio, creating a seamless connection between the indoor and outdoor spaces. A single door leads into the extended kitchen, which occupies the rear extension of the property. The kitchen features a fully tiled floor, an excellent selection of wall and floor storage units and extensive countertop space. Appliances include an integrated single oven, electric hob and overhead extractor fan. A dual stainless-steel sink with mixer tap is positioned beneath a window overlooking the rear garden and patio, while a further door provides direct access outside.\nCarpeted stairs rise to the first-floor landing, which is also carpeted and provides attic access. The main bedroom is positioned to the front of the property and features laminate flooring together with an impressive run of floor-to-ceiling fitted wardrobes extending across the width of the room, providing excellent storage. Bedroom Two is also finished with laminate flooring and built-in wardrobes, while a large picture window overlooks the agricultural fields to the rear, providing an attractive open outlook. Bedroom Three is a spacious bedroom featuring laminate flooring and built-in wardrobes. Completing the first-floor accommodation is a fully tiled family bathroom, fitted with a walk-in shower incorporating an electric shower unit, WC and wash hand basin.\nTo the front, a cobblelock driveway provides generous off-street parking for up to three family cars. \nThe rear garden is a particularly attractive feature of the property. A paved patio area is directly accessible from both the living room and kitchen, providing an ideal setting for outdoor dining and entertaining. Beyond the patio, the garden extends towards the rear boundary, where a superb chalet-style garden room is perfectly positioned.\nThis excellent self-contained unit is undoubtedly one of the property's most appealing features and offers tremendous versatility. Fully insulated, wired and plumbed, the garden room incorporates a kitchen/living area with floor-to-ceiling storage, a single oven, integrated electric hob, overhead extractor and sink with mixer tap. A separate room provides space for a bedroom, while an adjoining en-suite bathroom is fitted with WC, wash hand basin and electric walk-in shower. The garden room therefore offers a highly adaptable additional space that could accommodate extended family members, visiting guests, a home office, home gym, teenager's accommodation or additional recreational and leisure space. A small patio area leads from the entrance of the garden room, while the remainder of the garden is complemented by two spacious storage sheds, providing excellent additional storage.\nThe property enjoys an excellent position on Aylmer Road, within comfortable walking distance of Newcastle Village, providing convenient access to local shops, such as Lidl and Supervalu, schools and amenities."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 4.21m x 1.60m\nSpacious entrance hall with laminate flooring and under-stair storage.\n\nLiving Room - 2.76m x 4.0m\nBright living room with laminate flooring, large picture window and feature fireplace.\n\nGround Floor Bathroom - 1.35m x 2.67m\nFully tiled and fitted with electric shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nFamily Room - 3.75m x 5.86m\nSpacious full-width living room with feature fireplace and double doors leading to the rear patio.\n\nKitchen - 4.76m x 2.55m\nExtended kitchen with tiled flooring, wall and floor units, generous worktop space, integrated oven, electric hob and extractor fan. Dual stainless-steel sink with mixer tap and access to the rear patio.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.41m x 3.71m\nFront-facing bedroom with laminate flooring and extensive floor-to-ceiling fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.68m x 3.81m\nBedroom with laminate flooring, built-in wardrobes and large picture window overlooking the agricultural lands to the rear.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.0m x 2.50m\nSpacious bedroom with laminate flooring and built-in wardrobes.\n\nBathroom - 2.0m x 2.0m\nFully tiled bathroom with walk-in electric shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\n"
      },
